ted File with Text:\n```\nQuick QA Announcement Templates\n\nInstructions for use\n- Replace bracketed placeholders like [date], [time], [env], [product], [owner], [JIRA link], [contact].\n- Pick the scenario closest to your need and send on Slack/Email/Calendar as indicated.\n- Keep it under 80 words for Slack; include key impact and action required.\n\n1) QA Environment Maintenance/Downtime\n- Slack:\n  Heads up: QA [env] will be unavailable for maintenance on [date] from [start]\u2013[end] [timezone]. Impact: builds/tests paused. Action: wrap active runs before [cutoff]. Status will be posted here. Contact: [owner].\n- Email subject: QA [env] maintenance \u2013 [date] [start]\u2013[end] [timezone]\n- Email body:\n  Summary: QA [env] maintenance window on [date] [start]\u2013[end] [timezone].\n  Impact: Deployments, CI jobs, and manual testing paused.\n  Action: Finish runs by [cutoff]; reschedule jobs afterward.\n  Rollback/ETA: We\u2019ll confirm completion in channel; issues -> [contact].\n- Calendar invite title: QA [env] maintenance window\n- Invite description: Downtime for QA [env] to apply updates. Impact: testing paused. Owner: [owner].\n\n2) Test Freeze (Pre-release)\n- Slack:\n  Test Freeze starts [date time] for [product] release [version]. Only P0/P1 fixes allowed with QA approval. Please avoid new feature merges to [branch]. Questions: [contact].\n- Email subject: Test Freeze for [product] [version] starts [date]\n- Email body:\n  Window: [start] to [end].\n  Scope: No feature merges; P0/P1 bug fixes with approval.\n  Criteria to lift: All P1s closed, no open blockers, CI green for 24h.\n  Contacts: Eng: [name], QA: [name].\n\n3) Bug Bash Invite\n- Slack:\n  Join our Bug Bash for [product] [version] on [date] [time\u2013time] [timezone]. Focus areas: [areas]. Guide: [doc link]. Sign-up: [sheet]. Swag/prizes for top finders. Contact: [owner].\n- Email subject: Bug Bash \u2013 [product] [version], [date]\n- Email body:\n  When/Where: [date/time], [location/Zoom].\n  Scenarios: [areas]. How to report: [JIRA/board link].\n  Scoring & prizes: [details].\n  Prep: Latest build: [build link].\n\n4) Release Candidate Validation Start\n- Slack:\n  RC validation for [product] [version] starts now. Build: [link]. Test plan: [link]. Target GA: [date]. Please report issues to [JIRA link] using label [label]. Contact: [owner].\n- Email subject: RC validation kicked off \u2013 [product] [version]\n- Email body:\n  Scope: [components].\n  Entry criteria met: [list].\n  Exit criteria: 0 blockers, P1<= [n], test pass rate >= [x]%. \n  Reporting: [JIRA link/labels].\n\n5) Critical Defect Advisory\n- Slack:\n  Alert: Critical defect [ID] affects [scope]. Workaround: [steps]/None. Fix ETA: [date time]. Impacted: [teams/features]. Track here: [JIRA link]. Contact: [owner].\n- Email subject: Critical defect [ID] impacting [scope] \u2013 ETA [date]\n- Email body:\n  Issue: [summary].\n  Impact: [who/what].\n  Workaround: [steps]/None.\n  Next update: [cadence].\n  Owner: [owner].\n\n6) Test Data Refresh\n- Slack:\n  Test data refresh in QA [env] on [date time]. Expect data reset for [systems]. Backup snapshots at [location] until [retention]. Contact: [owner].\n- Email subject: QA [env] test data refresh \u2013 [date]\n- Email body:\n  Scope: [systems/tables].\n  Impact: Test accounts and datasets reset.\n  Action: Export any needed data before [cutoff].\n  Restore: Snapshot at [path] until [retention].\n\nDistribution guidance\n- Slack channels: #engineering, #qa, #release, team-specific channels.\n- Email lists: eng-all@[company], qa@[company], release@[company], product@[company].\n- Calendar: Invite involved squads only; mark as FYI when no attendance needed.\n- Timing: Post 24\u201348h in advance for planned work; ASAP for incidents with updates every [30/60] min.\n\nApproval workflow\n- Draft by QA owner -> Review by Eng lead/PM (as needed) -> Post/send.\n- For incidents: incident commander approves; skip review if time-critical.